      "writtenOn": "2025-05-23T00:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Took me a while to understand that MapAtCreationInternal was faking SetInitialized in order to skip initialization here. It\u0027s unintuitive that IsInitialized is true when initialization hasn\u0027t occurred yet (it actually happens when the staging buffer gets copied into the main buffer), though this was already how it worked (via SetInitialized just below). But at least we could localize that logic to just this one function. WDYT of instead passing a bool out from MapAtCreationInternal telling us whether a staging buffer is in use?\n\n```\n// If a staging buffer is in use, the main buffer will actually get initialized when\n// the staging data is copied in. (But we mark the main buffer as initialized now.)\nif (!usingStagingBuffer) {\n```",
